invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_word.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the square of four words doubles the sum of the products a_i a_j
  without the bit that crosses from word 4 into word 5, so a square whose
  word 4 has its top bit set is short by 2^320. bin/p256_equiv_test holds
  every square to p256_field.c's and every inverse to p256_field.c's and
  p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    uint64_t d5 = (s5 << 1) | (s4 >> 63);
--- new
    uint64_t d5 = s5 << 1;
